CORE libcxx no-vacuity-check
main.cpp
--cpp11 --stdlib libc++ --object-bits 12 --depth 400
^VERIFICATION
^EXIT=(0|10)$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
Round 163d: the stream sentry (a member class of basic_ostream defined
outside it, [temp.mem.class]/1) is no longer dropped, so its constructor
and the tie()/flush() and locale code behind it are executed; the lower --depth
(400, was 1000) keeps symbolic execution within the time limit.
no-vacuity-check: a conversion check (any verdict); with bounds that reach
the end of main, symbolic execution of the stream output exceeds 300 s.
Root cause: `std::cerr << std::endl' resolves to operator<<(bool) with
the address of endl<wchar_t> (the conversion of an overload set to bool
is not possible, [over.over]/1), and only when the source file is named
main.cpp or a.cpp; the resulting narrow() loop in ctype<char> runs to its
bound.
